{
 "kind": "climate-axes",
 "purpose": "Which climate axis a dimension's noise router actually varies across its playable radius, so an explicit biome band (T19) is written on an axis the world crosses.",
 "method": "customdim sample-noise at 11 points along a diagonal spanning the full playable radius of one representative dimension per (type, noiseSettings). Ranked by span x (distinct/samples), so a wide-but-degenerate axis loses to a narrower smooth one.",
 "limits": [
  "One representative per combination, not per dimension. Treat a row as the STARTING POINT and measure your own dimension before relying on it: the_crumbling_reaches (end, border 2048) measures weirdness 1.099 / continentalness 0.895, the reverse of the end row's representative.",
  "Rank by distribution, not span. adventure:void gives weirdness a span of 2.000 across just THREE distinct values (7 of 11 samples pinned at -0.50) - the widest span and the worst axis.",
  "overworld, checkerboard and superflat answer 'Not a MultiNoiseBiomeSource' and have no climate point to band on.",
  "perDimension entries are measured at that dimension's OWN borders.player and are ground truth for it; the `axes` list above is a per-(type, noiseSettings) fallback for a dimension not measured directly.",
  "axes[].all now carries min/max from the representative's own samples, so check-band-reach.py can give an INDICATIVE verdict for a dimension with no per-dimension measurement. Indicative only: span scales with radius, and the representative may sit at a different border."
 ],
 "regenerate": "Load each representative with `customdim load <slug>`, then sample; see .handoff/ for the harness used.",
